  "term": "M–C SDS",
  "definition": "M–C SDS refers to a short-form social desirability scale, an assessment used to measure a person’s tendency to give socially desirable responses. In the study packet, it was included alongside other questionnaires to examine how self-forgiveness relates to social desirability.",
